# LeetCode 137 – Single Number II

**Problem:** Every element appears exactly 3 times except one element, which appears only once. Find the single element.

## 1. Sorting Approach

**Logic:**
- Sort the array.
- Check adjacent elements.
- If `nums[i] != nums[i+1]`, return `nums[i]`.
- Otherwise, skip the next 3 occurrences using `i += 3`.
- If the loop finishes, return the last element.

**Code:**
```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int singleNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        int i = 0;
        int n = nums.size();

        while(i < n - 1) {
            if(nums[i] != nums[i + 1]) {
                return nums[i];
            }

            i += 3;
        }

        return nums[n - 1];
    }
};
```

**Complexity:**
- Time: O(N log N)
- Space: O(1) auxiliary space (excluding sorting implementation details).

